# Full scripted session against: claude --ax-screen-reader
# Every Enter is a separate write: a chunk that contains text plus CR is treated as a paste.
mark
wait 8000 Yes, I trust this folder
iffound send y
iffound sleep 150
iffound send \r
wait 6000 Keep xhigh
iffound send n
iffound sleep 150
iffound send \r
quiet 2500 30000

# Question 1: plain
send What is 2+2? Answer in one short line.
sleep 150
send \r
mark
wait 90000 \x07
quiet 2000 20000

# Question 2: markdown structure
send Write a short markdown answer with two level-2 headings and a three item bullet list about the color blue.
sleep 150
send \r
mark
wait 90000 \x07
quiet 2000 20000

# Tool use; may trigger a permission prompt
send Create a file named hello.txt in this folder containing the single word hi.
sleep 150
send \r
mark
wait 90000 \x07
quiet 2000 20000
wait 500 Enter selection
iffound send 1
iffound sleep 150
iffound send \r
iffound mark
iffound wait 90000 \x07
quiet 2000 20000
wait 500 Enter y/n
iffound send y
iffound sleep 150
iffound send \r
iffound mark
iffound wait 90000 \x07
quiet 2000 20000

# Multi-line input via bracketed paste, then Enter separately
send \e[200~Reply with the word RECEIVED and say how many lines this message has.\nThis is the second line.\e[201~
sleep 150
send \r
mark
wait 90000 \x07
quiet 2000 20000

# Bare Enter on an empty prompt, then exit
send \r
sleep 500
send /exit
sleep 150
send \r
exit 15000
